# Weekly sweep for T-NNNN ids cited in COMMIT MESSAGES that did not exist yet
# (T-2300). Sibling of pantheon-cited-hash-lint (T-2272): same defect class — a
# citation that silently resolves to the wrong thing rather than to nothing.
#
# ⚠️ WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE UNIT AND NOT A SECOND ExecStart ON THE HASH LINT.
# The ask was to compose the two, and conceptually they are one job. But both
# exit 1 on findings, and a Type=oneshot stops at the first failing ExecStart —
# so merging them would mean any unreachable-hash finding silently prevented the
# ticket-citation sweep from running at all. Prefixing with `-` to ignore the
# failure would instead break OnFailure and retire the alerting for both. Two
# units keep each sweep's verdict its own; the composition is in the tooling and
# the schedule, not in a shared exit code.
#
# ⚠️ A SWEEP, NOT A PRE-COMMIT GATE — but for a DIFFERENT reason than the hash
# lint's. The hash lint cannot be a gate because the rebase creates the defect
# after the check. This one COULD be a commit-time gate: at commit time the id
# either exists or it does not. It is deliberately not one yet, because a hook
# that refuses commits is fleet-wide blast radius on a tool with one day of
# history, and the failure it prevents is a record-quality defect rather than an
# incident. Revisit once the sweep has run clean for a while.
#
# Read-only: it reports, commits nothing, and touches no ticket.
[Unit]
Description=Pantheon cited-ticket lint — weekly forward-reference sweep
Documentation=file:///home/%u/pantheon-config/tools/cited_ticket_lint.py
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

OnFailure=pantheon-unit-failure-alert@%n.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=%h/pantheon-config
Environment=PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
ExecStart=/usr/bin/python3 %h/pantheon-config/tools/cited_ticket_lint.py --limit 1000
StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal
TimeoutStartSec=15min

[Install]
WantedBy=default.target
